      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "# Polaris ClickHouse\n\n**v1 posture.** Polaris does **not** scrape ClickHouse natively in v1 (the `clickhouse` service in `docker-compose.yml` does not expose `/metrics`). The dashboard's signals come from two places: **clickhouse-sink**, the only process that writes to ClickHouse, which is the only process that writes to ClickHouse.\n\n**Two ingestion paths.** The sink routes by stream family into two interface tables, and every sink series carries a `table` label so they are read separately:\n\n- `analytics_events_queue` \u2014 source events from `resolved.events`, landing in `analytics_ingest_log` + `analytics_raw`.\n- `analytics_processed_queue` \u2014 derived events from `session` / `identity` / `attribution`.events, landing in `analytics_processed`.\n\n**Available metrics**:\n\n- `polaris_clickhouse_sink_lag_seconds{table}` \u2014 ingestion lag: now \u2212 the envelope's `ingested_at` for the last row written. Powers the warn and page alerts.\n- `polaris_clickhouse_sink_rows_consumed_total{project_id, environment, table}` \u2014 rows inserted.\n- `polaris_clickhouse_sink_rows_skipped_total` \u2014 messages the sink could not project onto a row. The only path where an event leaves the pipeline without reaching ClickHouse, a DLQ, or an ingester rejection; alerted above 1/min.\n- `polaris_clickhouse_sink_batches_total{table}` and `polaris_clickhouse_sink_insert_duration_ms_last{table}` \u2014 batch shape and INSERT latency.\n- `polaris_clickhouse_sink_insert_failures_total{table}` \u2014 rejected INSERTs. With `materialized_views_ignore_errors` at 0, a materialized view that throws fails its source table's INSERT, so this is the MV-failure signal. The old `polaris_clickhouse_mv_state` polled `system.view_refreshes`, which covers refreshable MVs only and never had a value here.\n- `polaris_clickhouse_operator_raw_query_total{caller}` \u2014 operator escape-hatch raw queries (audit signal).\n\n`polaris_clickhouse_kafka_ingestion_lag_seconds` is **gone**: ClickHouse stopped consuming for itself at the RabbitMQ migration, so `system.kafka_consumers` is empty. Panels that used it now read the sink's own lag.\n\n**Not on this dashboard yet:** the sink's own retry/DLQ depth. Two panels read `polaris_processor_events_*{processor_name=\"analytics-projector\"}` until 126EPNIQ retired that processor; the sink keeps its own `SinkMetrics` and emits no processor-tier counters, so those panels were removed rather than repointed at a metric that does not exist.\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.4.0",
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
    },
